# Rec Room private-server hostnames.
#
# Rec Room does not talk to one host. Its service-discovery document advertises a family of
# subdomains (accounts, auth, api, cdn, ...) and the client then calls them literally. So this list
# is inherently open-ended, and a missing entry shows up as one broken feature rather than a startup
# error.
#
# The list below mirrors ServiceCatalog.Labels in the server exactly: every advertised label gets an
# entry. Add to both together, not one alone.
#
# 127.0.0.1 is the default because this is a single-machine deployment. Use the machine's LAN
# address instead if the game runs elsewhere, or the reverse proxy's address if it runs in a
# container.
#
# Requires administrator rights to edit, and is required at all: without it the client resolves
# rec.local through public DNS, gets NXDOMAIN, and fails before any of the mod's patches matter.

# Apex and discovery hosts.
127.0.0.1	rec.local
127.0.0.1	ns.rec.local

# Advertised service hosts, matching ServiceCatalog.Labels.
127.0.0.1	accounts.rec.local
127.0.0.1	ai.rec.local
127.0.0.1	api.rec.local
127.0.0.1	auth.rec.local
127.0.0.1	bugreporting.rec.local
127.0.0.1	cards.rec.local
127.0.0.1	cdn.rec.local
127.0.0.1	chat.rec.local
127.0.0.1	clubs.rec.local
127.0.0.1	cms.rec.local
127.0.0.1	commerce.rec.local
127.0.0.1	data.rec.local
127.0.0.1	datacollection.rec.local
127.0.0.1	discovery.rec.local
127.0.0.1	econ.rec.local
127.0.0.1	gamelogs.rec.local
127.0.0.1	geo.rec.local
127.0.0.1	img.rec.local
127.0.0.1	leaderboard.rec.local
127.0.0.1	link.rec.local
127.0.0.1	lists.rec.local
127.0.0.1	match.rec.local
127.0.0.1	moderation.rec.local
127.0.0.1	notify.rec.local
127.0.0.1	platformnotifications.rec.local
127.0.0.1	playersettings.rec.local
127.0.0.1	roomcomments.rec.local
127.0.0.1	roomieintegrations.rec.local
127.0.0.1	rooms.rec.local
127.0.0.1	storage.rec.local
127.0.0.1	strings.rec.local
127.0.0.1	strings-cdn.rec.local
127.0.0.1	studio.rec.local
127.0.0.1	thorn.rec.local
127.0.0.1	videos.rec.local
127.0.0.1	www.rec.local